editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.md:85:The three primary working measures all pass: sentence mean, ≥40-word share, and words per scene. The main formula concern is therefore not scene scale or missing long sentences; it is the low median and narrow overall spread. Any repair should join only adjacent narration or explanatory fragments that are already one thought. It should not touch the concise dialogue, protected wording, or fight landings, and it should not attempt to manufacture a population SD of 26.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.md:104:2. **Location:** Select explanatory runs in chapters 16 and 19, and the four-part argument in chapter 20; exclude protected text, dialogue landings, and both physical encounters. **Observed issue:** sentence mean 13.11 is at the low edge of the working range, median is 9 against 11, and population spread is 11.35 against ~26; some procedural thought arrives as strings of short units while paragraph blocks remain long. **Effect on the reader:** the prose is very clear, but portions can sound itemized and rhythmically flatter than the formula requests, especially aloud. **Proposed scope:** one manual sentence-level pass joining only adjacent clauses that form a single thought and adding paragraph turns where speaker, object, or inference changes; do not chase the SD target, lengthen dialogue, add jargon, or shorten scenes. Re-run the supplied metrics once. **Strength to preserve:** the clean thirteen-year-old accessibility, distinct voices, exact legal consequences, 3.5% long-sentence share, and the developed action.
