editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-001/AUTHORSHIP.md:17:**One session.** One author drafted all seven chapters in one session and one context. No other model drafted any part of them, and no subagents were used. No git command was run. Nothing outside the seven manuscript chapters and this movement's state folder was edited. `protected-patterns.txt` was not touched; the proposed patterns were tested from a scratch copy in the session scratchpad.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-001/AUTHORSHIP.md:26:**Method.** After the source read I wrote a private event list (`state/movement-001/EVENT-LIST.md`) and drafted from it and BOOK_MAP; the source chapters were not reopened. Each chapter was probed with `skeleton_probe.py` right after its first draft, and every listed pair was rebuilt unless it was protected or Tier B text.
