editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:21:| 19 | The Shape | 4,687 | 5 | **Day 49 supper.** The Ternhall keeper's private letter: Karis's transfer file requested — **"That's twice."** Seln's **beans**, laid right to left: Ternhall; Velmere's provincial registry; Lira's certification at the district seat *for completeness*; the house's own counter (item four); the coats now hold the road; "One query is a clerk… Four… is somebody's plan." Lira: the Fenmark line under the corrections — "Put it in your column." Brom: **"Does the query show at the estate's end?"** — the head of his house is on the file. Karis rules **one empty line**. Two hours later **Hesk's letter** in the evening post, opened walking (the surveyor's level set back a hair wrong because the whole valley agrees with it; the widow's dog), then **read aloud at the window** — **the protected paragraph**. *Grew up in it*: the shavings under the bench, the tin box. Lira: "Denvash." Seln's fifth bean apart; Karis fills the line. **"Walking the fences" / pre-restriction inventory**: before the ruling; "Nine weeks. They are in the sixth."; five dull files, an afternoon to assemble. Karis: the ninth heading, *other relationships* — what he'd mind; Brom: "Said." Lira takes a bean: **"The question is what we do the day after."** Seln's stillness. **Withrow** reads the letter (twelve breaths; stops for nine); the brown pocket code; the haulier's story **told from the flour sack backward** — nine letters in the order they came; Force, Bronze Rank Four; the station slip twenty years old; two frames silent; seven weeks of careful work; one trouble in nine coats; east past the last station in eighteen months; the daughter at her counter; *grew up in it* under the ninth heading; **"Not a hand on the door. A hand on the clock."**; choosing, dearer tonight. Log: the first pole cracks — the line between the system and the people can't be found. |
