editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/B5-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:267:B5 canon: Hesk's reply, road day eleven, written off the broadsides and sent to meet the column, verbatim (ch60:163, protected B5 §10 item 57): *Third on the continent, and the judges wrote "no number goes here." Your grandmother would have had that framed. Seventeen, unmeasured, and true. Come home when the road allows. — H.*; slid "behind the old volume's front board, with the other letters that lived there" (ch60:165). Cael's own letters to Hesk (six pages; "It turns out I like the company", ch60:43) and to Vell (ending *Your ledger rated me before any of theirs could. It's still the one I check the others against.*, ch60:47) went by Bracken's pouch on T26; no reply from Vell is on the page. The year's ledger is in Hesk's book (ch60:3–33, with the six guesses, the B4 minute and the costed rule); the old volume took the road's entries and is full, "its last leaf … until the line ran into the binding" on the last ferry (ch60:191). SL:89–90 (Hesk; Vell) hold.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/B5-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:287:B5 canon: "Rematch," she said. (ch59:183, the closing — protected item 57); "Find out what you are. Then find me. I want the rematch with whatever that is." (ch56:226, on the stone); "That was mine," — "A piece of it," said Cael. (ch56:210–216: the line is Cael's answer, "the truest thing he could give her without giving her the rest"); then hers: "Nineteen years. Nobody has ever shown me something I couldn't name." (ch56:222); her notebook line *Today somebody asked me something.* (ch57); her citation sealed in her case lining, unread; she "did not try to work out how he had done it". SL:88 ("An appointment, not a challenge.") holds. B6's statement ("Never. Not at Gold.", M3:69) and letter are B6's own and build on these; the reply at the Line (M9) answers the letter. Daeva nineteen; Gold Rank Three (ch54:99).
