editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-19.md-185-"He'd done nothing," said Withrow. "Twenty years before, a station clerk made a slip writing down his Kindling, and the one officer who could have sworn to the true reading was dead, so the slip could never be put right. The registry stood him in a frame again. Twice. Twice the frame had nothing to say. That was all." She touched the printed list beside her old note. "These are the nine headings. Employment, guild, credentials, property, debts, enrollments, travel, office, and *other relationships*. The district was short of clerks that year and I was good at it. I walked his fences myself. Seven weeks. I was proud of how careful it was."
