books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/chapters/chapter-05.md:39:The four days ran on the office's ordinary clock. The certification dispute from the coastal district was resolved by a two-line advisory. The stations-office staffing note was annotated and returned. On the third day a junior evaluator from the northern district came up to the corner office with a difficult file — a Kindling record that did not match its practitioner's demonstrated architecture by a margin the junior found troubling — and Vastin reviewed it with him for an hour, patiently, the way he had reviewed such files for thirty years: the architecture was within tolerance; the record was sound; the margin was the ordinary variance of a young practitioner developing faster than his evaluators expected; continue observation. The junior thanked him and went down, reassured. Vastin sat afterward with the file's copy for longer than the file warranted, and could not have said why, and entered the not-saying in no ledger, because it was not yet a thing with a shape.
